Here's my appraisal:

8BIT Theatre - Aack! Internet humor! ...well, NetHack already
references the Usenet Oracle, but that's because NetHack sprang (fully
armed) from Usenet's loins, and thus takes some props from it.

Dudley's Dungeon - flattering though it may be, it does _not_ bode well
to create a causal content loop like this. As in "NetHack does this
because Dudley's Dungeon did that because NetHack did this..."

Wesnoth - you know what I wish? I wish that NetHack would include some
reference to Scarab of RA (a very roguelike-inspired game only
available for 80's Macs. It's got a Wikipedia article.)

Scud: Disposible Assassin - nah.

Schlock Mercenary - double nah - there's too many layers of separation
from NetHack (chaotic fantasy roguelike) to Schlock (neutral sf
webcomic). At least with 8Bit you've got the same genre.

Gary Larson - what about that episode when the dragons admit that they
have to get a "real" princess, instead of a log with a face drawn on?
But apart from that, nah.

Iain M. Banks - Lazy Gun, you say?
(http://groups.google.com/group/rec.games.roguelike.nethack/browse_thread/thread/d2b58f61b9d0f0bf/873e4603b9407290?q=%22lazy+gun%22&rnum=2#873e4603b9407290)

His Dark Materials - well, we _can't_ include Aesahaettr as a weapon,
because the point of that weapon is that it's too powerful. So what's
left?



